{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-77471" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the minor of ${k}_{22}$ in the matrix\n$K=[\\begin{aligned}p & p & -p \\\\ -q & q & q \\\\ q & -2 & q\\end{aligned}]?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038872/state.json" "file_sha256" "3842f87edd643869f1639bc0ebc01369a8a356d427bbb6dcd10e60d7cb6b6981"} {"question" "q-77471" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we remove the second row and the second column:\n\n$$\nK=[\\begin{aligned}p & ∗ & -p \\\\ ∗ & q & ∗ \\\\ q & ∗ & q\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n \n\nNext, we calculate the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det[\\begin{aligned}p & -p \\\\ q & q\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}p & -p \\\\ q & q\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =p\\cdot p-q\\cdot (-p) \\\\  & =pq+pq \\\\  & =2pq\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038872/state.json" "file_sha256" "3842f87edd643869f1639bc0ebc01369a8a356d427bbb6dcd10e60d7cb6b6981"} {"question" "q-77471" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038872/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f0c38e6b302f592ad29f04aa7f573126a88390d519f0073cdf113bab797bd7dc"} {"question" "q-77471" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038872/state.json" "file_sha256" "3842f87edd643869f1639bc0ebc01369a8a356d427bbb6dcd10e60d7cb6b6981"} {"question" "q-77471" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "2pq"] ["math" "p-q"] ["math" "pq-1"] ["math" "q-p"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038872/state.json" "file_sha256" "3842f87edd643869f1639bc0ebc01369a8a356d427bbb6dcd10e60d7cb6b6981"} {"question" "q-77471" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2pq"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038872/state.json" "file_sha256" "3842f87edd643869f1639bc0ebc01369a8a356d427bbb6dcd10e60d7cb6b6981"} {"question" "q-48696" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The population $p$, in millions, of a particular colony of bacteria after $t$ days can be modeled by the function $p(t)=\\frac{{2}^{{t}^{2}+1}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}.$ What is the instantaneous rate of change of the bacteria population as a function of $t?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038872/state.json" "file_sha256" "3842f87edd643869f1639bc0ebc01369a8a356d427bbb6dcd10e60d7cb6b6981"} {"question" "q-48696" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The instantaneous rate of change of the bacteria population is equal to ${p}^{′}(t).$ \n\nFirst, we take the derivative and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{p}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{{2}^{{t}^{2}+1}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{2}^{{t}^{2}+1}\\cdot (2t)\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\  & =2t\\cdot {2}^{{t}^{2}+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038872/state.json" "file_sha256" "3842f87edd643869f1639bc0ebc01369a8a356d427bbb6dcd10e60d7cb6b6981"} {"question" "q-48696" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038872/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f0c38e6b302f592ad29f04aa7f573126a88390d519f0073cdf113bab797bd7dc"} {"question" "q-48696" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038872/state.json" "file_sha256" "3842f87edd643869f1639bc0ebc01369a8a356d427bbb6dcd10e60d7cb6b6981"} {"question" "q-48696" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$2\\cdot {2}^{{t}^{2}+1}$ million bacteria per day"] ["text" "$2\\cdot {2}^{{t}^{3}}$ million bacteria per day"] ["text" "$2t\\cdot {2}^{{t}^{2}+1}$ million bacteria per day"] ["text" "$\\frac{1}{t}\\cdot {2}^{{t}^{2}+1}$ million bacteria per day"] ["text" "${2}^{{t}^{2}+1}$ million bacteria per day"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038872/state.json" "file_sha256" "3842f87edd643869f1639bc0ebc01369a8a356d427bbb6dcd10e60d7cb6b6981"} {"question" "q-48696" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$2t\\cdot {2}^{{t}^{2}+1}$ million bacteria per day"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038872/state.json" "file_sha256" "3842f87edd643869f1639bc0ebc01369a8a356d427bbb6dcd10e60d7cb6b6981"} {"question" "q-332175" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Express $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-{210}^{∘})$ in terms of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$\n\n$\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-{210}^{∘})=$\n{{field-1}}$\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,+$\n{{field-2}}$\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038872/state.json" "file_sha256" "3842f87edd643869f1639bc0ebc01369a8a356d427bbb6dcd10e60d7cb6b6981"} {"question" "q-332175" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall the difference formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u-v)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v-\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nApplying the difference formula for sine with $u=x$ and $v={210}^{∘},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-{210}^{∘}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡{210}^{∘}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡{210}^{∘} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot (-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038872/state.json" "file_sha256" "3842f87edd643869f1639bc0ebc01369a8a356d427bbb6dcd10e60d7cb6b6981"} {"question" "q-332175" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038872/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f0c38e6b302f592ad29f04aa7f573126a88390d519f0073cdf113bab797bd7dc"} {"question" "q-332175" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038872/state.json" "file_sha256" "3842f87edd643869f1639bc0ebc01369a8a356d427bbb6dcd10e60d7cb6b6981"} {"question" "q-332175" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038872/state.json" "file_sha256" "3842f87edd643869f1639bc0ebc01369a8a356d427bbb6dcd10e60d7cb6b6981"} {"question" "q-332175" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038872/state.json" "file_sha256" "3842f87edd643869f1639bc0ebc01369a8a356d427bbb6dcd10e60d7cb6b6981"} {"question" "q-332175" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038872/state.json" "file_sha256" "3842f87edd643869f1639bc0ebc01369a8a356d427bbb6dcd10e60d7cb6b6981"} {"question" "q-142835" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\frac{2{sec}^{2}⁡x-1}{1+2{tan}^{2}⁡x}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038872/state.json" "file_sha256" "3842f87edd643869f1639bc0ebc01369a8a356d427bbb6dcd10e60d7cb6b6981"} {"question" "q-142835" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's recall the secant-tangent identity:\n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nWe rewrite the given expression using the secant-tangent identity as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2\\,{sec}^{2}⁡x-1}{1+2{tan}^{2}⁡x} & =\\frac{2\\,(1+{tan}^{2}⁡x)-1}{1+2{tan}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{2+2{tan}^{2}⁡x-1}{1+2{tan}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1+2{tan}^{2}⁡x}{1+2{tan}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{1+2{tan}^{2}⁡x}}{\\cancel{1+2{tan}^{2}⁡x}} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{2{sec}^{2}⁡x-1}{1+2{tan}^{2}⁡x}=1.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038872/state.json" "file_sha256" "3842f87edd643869f1639bc0ebc01369a8a356d427bbb6dcd10e60d7cb6b6981"} {"question" "q-142835" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038872/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f0c38e6b302f592ad29f04aa7f573126a88390d519f0073cdf113bab797bd7dc"} {"question" "q-142835" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038872/state.json" "file_sha256" "3842f87edd643869f1639bc0ebc01369a8a356d427bbb6dcd10e60d7cb6b6981"} {"question" "q-142835" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "1+2\\operatorname{tan}⁡x"] ["math" "1-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x"] ["math" "2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038872/state.json" "file_sha256" "3842f87edd643869f1639bc0ebc01369a8a356d427bbb6dcd10e60d7cb6b6981"} {"question" "q-142835" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038872/state.json" "file_sha256" "3842f87edd643869f1639bc0ebc01369a8a356d427bbb6dcd10e60d7cb6b6981"} {"question" "q-242909" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Expressed in terms of natural logarithms, determine the value of $x$ that satisfies the equation ${e}^{x}={9}^{5-x}.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038872/state.json" "file_sha256" "3842f87edd643869f1639bc0ebc01369a8a356d427bbb6dcd10e60d7cb6b6981"} {"question" "q-242909" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we take the natural logarithm $(ln)$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x} & ={9}^{5-x} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{x}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({9}^{5-x})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the fact that $\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{a})=a$ to simplify the left-hand side. This gives\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({9}^{5-x}).\n$$\n\nNext, we use the power law of logarithms to simplify the right-hand side:\n\n$$\nx=(5-x)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(9)\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =(5-x)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(9) \\\\ x & =5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(9)-x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(9) \\\\ x+x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(9) & =5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(9) \\\\ x(1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(9)) & =5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(9) \\\\ x & =\\frac{5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(9)}{1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(9)}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038872/state.json" "file_sha256" "3842f87edd643869f1639bc0ebc01369a8a356d427bbb6dcd10e60d7cb6b6981"} {"question" "q-242909" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038872/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f0c38e6b302f592ad29f04aa7f573126a88390d519f0073cdf113bab797bd7dc"} {"question" "q-242909" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038872/state.json" "file_sha256" "3842f87edd643869f1639bc0ebc01369a8a356d427bbb6dcd10e60d7cb6b6981"} {"question" "q-242909" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5\\ln(9)}{1+\\ln(9)}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038872/state.json" "file_sha256" "3842f87edd643869f1639bc0ebc01369a8a356d427bbb6dcd10e60d7cb6b6981"} {"question" "q-115309" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the center of the ellipse $\\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y-6)^{2}}{36}=1?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038872/state.json" "file_sha256" "3842f87edd643869f1639bc0ebc01369a8a356d427bbb6dcd10e60d7cb6b6981"} {"question" "q-115309" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have $h=-4$ and $k=6,$ so the center is located at $(-4,6).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038872/state.json" "file_sha256" "3842f87edd643869f1639bc0ebc01369a8a356d427bbb6dcd10e60d7cb6b6981"} {"question" "q-115309" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038872/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f0c38e6b302f592ad29f04aa7f573126a88390d519f0073cdf113bab797bd7dc"} {"question" "q-115309" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038872/state.json" "file_sha256" "3842f87edd643869f1639bc0ebc01369a8a356d427bbb6dcd10e60d7cb6b6981"} {"question" "q-115309" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-4,6)"] ["math" "(2,6)"] ["math" "(4,-6)"] ["math" "(6,-2)"] ["math" "(6,-4)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038872/state.json" "file_sha256" "3842f87edd643869f1639bc0ebc01369a8a356d427bbb6dcd10e60d7cb6b6981"} {"question" "q-115309" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(-4,6)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038872/state.json" "file_sha256" "3842f87edd643869f1639bc0ebc01369a8a356d427bbb6dcd10e60d7cb6b6981"} {"question" "q-115699" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A right Riemann sum is used to approximate the area under the curve $y=f(x)$ between $x=-4$ and $x=-1$ for each of the functions below. For which function does the Riemann sum give an *underestimate* of the area?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038872/state.json" "file_sha256" "3842f87edd643869f1639bc0ebc01369a8a356d427bbb6dcd10e60d7cb6b6981"} {"question" "q-115699" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The right Riemann sum underestimates the area under the respective curve if the function is decreasing over the given interval. \n\nOf the given options, the only function that is decreasing over $x\\in [-4,-1]$ is as follows.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038872/assets/8361d4cb197686b79cf21cb88ee70de5b3578e92fb758fb84aec754871dfca3e.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038872/state.json" "file_sha256" "3842f87edd643869f1639bc0ebc01369a8a356d427bbb6dcd10e60d7cb6b6981"} {"question" "q-115699" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038872/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f0c38e6b302f592ad29f04aa7f573126a88390d519f0073cdf113bab797bd7dc"} {"question" "q-115699" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038872/state.json" "file_sha256" "3842f87edd643869f1639bc0ebc01369a8a356d427bbb6dcd10e60d7cb6b6981"} {"question" "q-115699" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038872/assets/7c79516ab4216ae1eed208c87204ae045b7f070f13d98853d6fed56eaae9b1c6.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038872/assets/8361d4cb197686b79cf21cb88ee70de5b3578e92fb758fb84aec754871dfca3e.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038872/assets/9e57c21db9ca295e246eee4510497763c857d280338aba261a3f1c6fb309da9d.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038872/assets/a20867cc6aca9f9b9a5b2b5780597938f43547380a6a0294671660f4a982383a.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038872/assets/a4dc3b8db26fe963aca60dab6fd927581896329e1801c11ce2687be251d65840.png"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038872/state.json" "file_sha256" "3842f87edd643869f1639bc0ebc01369a8a356d427bbb6dcd10e60d7cb6b6981"} {"question" "q-115699" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/image "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038872/assets/8361d4cb197686b79cf21cb88ee70de5b3578e92fb758fb84aec754871dfca3e.png"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038872/state.json" "file_sha256" "3842f87edd643869f1639bc0ebc01369a8a356d427bbb6dcd10e60d7cb6b6981"} {"question" "q-40178" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the infinite geometric sequence that has a fourth term equal to $24$ and a seventh term equal to $\\frac{3}{8}.$ What is the sum to infinity of the terms of this sequence?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038872/state.json" "file_sha256" "3842f87edd643869f1639bc0ebc01369a8a356d427bbb6dcd10e60d7cb6b6981"} {"question" "q-40178" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The sum to infinity ${S}_{\\infty }$ of a geometric series is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{\\infty }=\\frac{{a}_{1}}{1-r},\\,|r|<1,\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term and $r$ is the common ratio.\n\nFrom the question statement we have ${a}_{4}=24$ and ${a}_{7}=\\frac{3}{8}.$ We can find the common ratio using the following formula:\n\n$$\n{r}^{n-m}=\\frac{{a}_{n}}{{a}_{m}}\n$$\n\nSubstituting in the known information into the above gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{7-4} & =\\frac{(\\frac{3}{8})}{24} \\\\ {r}^{3} & =(\\frac{3}{8})(\\frac{1}{24}) \\\\ {r}^{3} & =\\frac{1}{64} \\\\ {r}^{3} & ={(\\frac{1}{4})}^{3} \\\\ r & =\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}={a}_{1}{r}^{n-1}\n$$\n\nfor the $n$th term of the geometric sequence, we can find the first term. Indeed, for $n=4$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{4} & ={a}_{1}(r)^{3} \\\\ 24 & ={a}_{1}{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{3} \\\\ 24 & ={a}_{1}(\\frac{1}{64}) \\\\ {a}_{1} & =1\\,536\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, using the formula, we find that the sum to infinity is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{\\infty } & =\\frac{{a}_{1}}{1-r} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\,536}{(1-\\frac{1}{4})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\,536}{(\\frac{3}{4})} \\\\  & =1\\,536(\\frac{4}{3}) \\\\  & =2\\,048.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038872/state.json" "file_sha256" "3842f87edd643869f1639bc0ebc01369a8a356d427bbb6dcd10e60d7cb6b6981"} {"question" "q-40178" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038872/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f0c38e6b302f592ad29f04aa7f573126a88390d519f0073cdf113bab797bd7dc"} {"question" "q-40178" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038872/state.json" "file_sha256" "3842f87edd643869f1639bc0ebc01369a8a356d427bbb6dcd10e60d7cb6b6981"} {"question" "q-40178" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1\\,024"] ["math" "2\\,048"] ["math" "3\\,072"] ["math" "4\\,364"] ["math" "6\\,144"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038872/state.json" "file_sha256" "3842f87edd643869f1639bc0ebc01369a8a356d427bbb6dcd10e60d7cb6b6981"} {"question" "q-40178" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2\\,048"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038872/state.json" "file_sha256" "3842f87edd643869f1639bc0ebc01369a8a356d427bbb6dcd10e60d7cb6b6981"} {"question" "q-54161" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A curve is defined by the parametric equations $x={t}^{2}-1,\\,y=4{t}^{5}+1$ where $t$ is a real number. Calculate $\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038872/state.json" "file_sha256" "3842f87edd643869f1639bc0ebc01369a8a356d427bbb6dcd10e60d7cb6b6981"} {"question" "q-54161" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the first derivative, we will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=2t,\\,{y}^{′}(t)=20{t}^{4}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{20{t}^{4}}{2t}=10{t}^{3}.\n$$\n\nTo compute the second derivative, we can use the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{\\frac{d}{dt}(\\frac{dy}{dx})}{(\\frac{dx}{dt})}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{\\frac{d}{dt}(10{t}^{3})}{2t} \\\\  & =\\frac{30{t}^{2}}{2t} \\\\  & =15t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038872/state.json" "file_sha256" "3842f87edd643869f1639bc0ebc01369a8a356d427bbb6dcd10e60d7cb6b6981"} {"question" "q-54161" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038872/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f0c38e6b302f592ad29f04aa7f573126a88390d519f0073cdf113bab797bd7dc"} {"question" "q-54161" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038872/state.json" "file_sha256" "3842f87edd643869f1639bc0ebc01369a8a356d427bbb6dcd10e60d7cb6b6981"} {"question" "q-54161" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "15t"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "60{t}^{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{15t}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{t}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038872/state.json" "file_sha256" "3842f87edd643869f1639bc0ebc01369a8a356d427bbb6dcd10e60d7cb6b6981"} {"question" "q-54161" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "15t"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038872/state.json" "file_sha256" "3842f87edd643869f1639bc0ebc01369a8a356d427bbb6dcd10e60d7cb6b6981"}] "usage" {"q-48696" []} "basis" 1349 "retractions" [[17592186078937 :question/problem "The population $p$, in millions, of a particular colony of bacteria after $t$ days can be modeled by the function $p(t) = \\frac{2^{t^{2} + 1}}{\\ln 2}$. What is the instantaneous rate of change of the bacteria population as a function of $t$?"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186076834 17592186076835 17592186076836 17592186076837 17592186076838] "immutable_fields" [[17592186076833 :answer-field/correct] [17592186076833 :answer-field/id] [17592186076833 :answer-field/key] [17592186076833 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
